# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Read by `pnpm logs`, which uses Node's own
# loader — an exported variable still wins over this file.
#
# NEVER give a secret in here a VITE_ prefix. Vite reads this same file and inlines every
# VITE_-prefixed value into the client bundle, which is published as a static asset: the
# name below is invisible to the page, but VITE_CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN would be served to
# every visitor. Nothing this project runs in the browser needs a secret.

# An API token with Account · Workers Observability · Read, for reading Workers Logs from
# the terminal (https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens). A `wrangler login` OAuth
# token is not enough: its scopes stop at the live tail. Only needed for `pnpm logs` —
# the dashboard's Observability tab reads the same logs over a browser login.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Optional. The account is already pinned as account_id in wrangler.jsonc; set this only
# to point somewhere else.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
